&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a DevRel Engineer to work inside the product teams building Vercel&#39;s agentic infrastructure: &lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/ai-gateway&quot;&gt;AI Gateway&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-sandbox&quot;&gt;Sandbox&lt;/a&gt;, and the primitives that come after them. You&#39;ll sit with product and engineering, build with these tools before anyone else can, and show the world what they make possible. You will report to the Head of AI Infrastructure and can be located anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re based within a pre-determined commuting distance of one of our offices (SF, NY, London, or Berlin), the role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday, even if the role is listed as remote. For location-specific details, please connect with our recruiting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When applying, include a link to something you made that taught developers something, a talk, a repo, a post, a video. Applications without one will not be considered.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build agents and applications on AI Gateway and Sandbox before they ship, then turn what you learn into demos, templates, and open source projects developers actually clone and run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach developers how to build with agentic infrastructure through writing, talks, videos, and live coding. You set the canonical examples the ecosystem emulates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the products themselves. You sit in the same planning meetings as the PMs and engineers, and your job is to hit the rough edges first and make sure they get fixed before launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the important pieces of launches: example repos, launch demos, docs contributions, and the first wave of answers when developers start asking questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the outside in: track how developers across the ecosystem are building agents, where they get stuck, and what they&#39;re reaching for that doesn&#39;t exist yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in engineering, DevRel, or DX roles, with software you can point to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and shipped AI applications or agents: you know tool calling, model routing, and sandboxed code execution from using them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong TypeScript, and you&#39;re at home in the Next.js and AI SDK ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a public body of work: talks, posts, open source, or videos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can take a half-finished API and produce a working demo and a clear explanation in the same week, often times the same day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve changed a product roadmap with developer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
