&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the Field Engineering Operations team, and set team structures, role definitions, and engagement models as Field Engineering grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run capacity planning, territory design, and resource allocation across the Americas, Europe, the Middle East and Africa (EMEA), and Asia-Pacific (APAC), in step with go-to-market (GTM) teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the pre-sales to post-sales lifecycle framework, including technical win and onboarding forecasts, go-live tracking, and consumption ramp measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the Field Engineering metrics, dashboards, and health scoring models that show team performance, account engagement, and customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in operations, strategy, or technical program leadership supporting field engineering, solutions, or customer-facing technical teams at high-growth SaaS companies, including 3+ years building and leading teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built operational frameworks for pre-sales and post-sales technical teams, including territory planning, capacity modeling, and compensation design, at companies with $100M+ annual recurring revenue (ARR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on Salesforce administration and architecture, including custom objects, flows, reporting, and integrations with ecosystem applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnered with VP-level technical leaders to turn org priorities into operational plans, delivered with Sales, Finance, Product, and Revenue Operations&lt;/li&gt;
