&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Manager to join our Product team. You will own Vercel&#39;s compute platform — Fluid compute, Vercel, Functions, Sandbox, and more — the layer that runs every workload our customers deploy. You will set the direction for how developers configure, scale, and run code on Vercel, from a single function, to multi-service architectures, to agents. You will report to the Product Lead and will be located in San Francisco, CA (hybrid).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel invested in its own microVM-based compute infrastructure externally called “Fluid compute”. Fluid changed what’s now possible to run on Vercel. For example, we’ve delivered Sandboxes, a new primitive to run untrusted and agent-generated code. We are just scratching the surface of what Fluid is can deliver. This is a senior role with wide latitude: you&#39;ll decide where that platform goes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re based within a pre-determined commuting distance of one of our offices (SF, NY, London, or Berlin), the role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday. If you&#39;re located beyond that distance, the role is fully remote. For location-specific details, please connect with our recruiting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision, strategy, and multi-year roadmap for Vercel&#39;s compute platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how Vercel serves AI and agent workloads, where long-running, I/O-bound, and code-executing tasks have a fundamentally different compute profile than traditional request/response traffic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the developer experience of running workloads on Vercel: resource model, attributes, API and config files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering on the performance and reliability bar for compute, including cold starts and creation time latency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define pricing for new products and resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the compute primitives that adjacent product areas build on, and work with those teams on what they need from the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Enterprise customers and the field on compute requirements that block adoption or scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and shipped infrastructure or developer platform products, ideally compute, serverless, containers, or runtime platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the technical depth to reason about concurrency, cold starts, isolation models, and the cost and performance tradeoffs of a compute platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have owned a platform area that other product teams build on, and set technical direction others adopted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with AI or agent workloads and how their resource profile differs from conventional web traffic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working directly with Enterprise customers on infrastructure requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience using usage and product analytics data to drive roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked at a cloud provider or on a serverless, container, or edge compute platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an engineering background or have built software yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked on multi-runtime platforms and the tradeoffs of supporting several language runtimes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked on sandboxing, isolation, or secure execution of untrusted code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
